@* Every page but the landing page renders inside the docs shell (Layout/DocsLayout.razor); the
   landing page and the error pages opt out with @layout MainLayout. After a navigation the page's
   own H1 takes focus, so a screen reader starts reading at the new page.

   NotFound is the router's page for a client-side navigation to an unknown route, and also the
   target the host re-executes a deep link it could not route to (UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute
   in the server's Program.cs), so both kinds of miss render the same page. *@

<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Routes).Assembly" NotFoundPage="typeof(Pages.NotFound)">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(Layout.DocsLayout)" />
        <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
    </Found>
</Router>
